<section class="section container security-policy" aria-labelledby="policy-overview">
    <div class="security-policy-intro">
        <div><span class="eyebrow">Before you begin</span><h2 class="display-heading" id="policy-overview">A clear boundary <em>for research.</em></h2></div>
        <p>Testing requires a written invitation from the SerendibBank assessment owner. The invitation must name the exact website address, testing dates, approved accounts and private reporting channel. A changing temporary URL does not extend permission to other websites or services.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="security-policy-grid">
        <article><span class="security-policy-number">01</span><h3>Included services</h3><p>When named in your invitation, you may assess the customer website and its same-origin API, including account access, registration, payments, documents, support and digital services. Use only the accounts assigned to you.</p></article>
        <article><span class="security-policy-number">02</span><h3>Services outside scope</h3><p>Staff and management workspaces require separate written approval. Cloudflare, email providers, maps, GitHub, the host computer, other virtual machines, SSH and database services are outside the website assessment.</p></article>
        <article><span class="security-policy-number">03</span><h3>Research conduct</h3><p>Keep testing controlled and limited to the supplied accounts. Do not disrupt availability, use social engineering, access another person's records, run destructive tests, or retain more information than is needed to show a finding.</p></article>
        <article><span class="security-policy-number">04</span><h3>Private reporting</h3><p>Send findings through the reporting channel in your invitation. Include the affected address, clear reproduction steps, the observed result and redacted evidence. Stop and report promptly if you encounter unexpected personal information or service disruption.</p></article>
    </div>
    <div class="security-policy-close"><h2>Disclosure</h2><p>Please allow the assessment owner to review and address a finding before sharing it publicly. This policy does not promise a reward or authorize testing outside an issued invitation.</p></div>
</section>
